# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: spawning 100 detached strands via detach(); each increments counter
#         twice with a 1s sleep in between; final value is 200 after 2s wait.
# blocked: named-function declarations are not supported at v1.0.
#          Probed: `function add2() { ... }` raises "use 'var name =
#          function(...){...}'".  Rewriting the body is most of the
#          activation; the 100-strand timing it needs is available now
#          that `## mode: file` pumps the scheduler on the real clock.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: separator-detach
#
# Reason:
#   detach() shipped v0.10.10 (D7-C ratify). The fixture requires the
#   T39 chk driver for wall-clock timing (sleep 1s / sleep 2s) across
#   100 concurrent strands. Per-feature coverage in detach_basic.chk.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when T39 chk driver lands):
# # var x = 0 | {};
# # function add2() { x++; sleep(1s); x++ } | {};
# # for (var i = 0; i < 100; i++) detach(add2());
# # sleep(2s);
# # x;
# # [00000001] 200
